      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "We start by using the coordinates given to determine the constants \\(a\\) and \\(b\\) in the equation of the line \\(y = ax + b\\).\n\nFirst, we substitute the point \\((4, 5)\\) into the equation:\n\\[\n5 = 4a + b\n\\]\n\nNext, we substitute the point \\((8, 17)\\) into the equation:\n\\[\n17 = 8a + b\n\\]\n\nWe now have a system of linear equations:\n1. \\(4a + b = 5\\)\n2. \\(8a + b = 17\\)\n\nTo eliminate \\(b\\), we subtract the first equation from the second:\n\\[\n(8a + b) - (4a + b) = 17 - 5\n\\]\n\\[\n8a + b - 4a - b = 12\n\\]\n\\[\n4a = 12\n\\]\n\\[\na = 3\n\\]\n\nNow that we have \\(a = 3\\), we substitute \\(a\\) back into the first equation to solve for \\(b\\):\n\\[\n4(3) + b = 5\n\\]\n\\[\n12 + b = 5\n\\]\n\\[\nb = 5 - 12\n\\]\n\\[\nb = -7\n\\]\n\nWe now have \\(a = 3\\) and \\(b = -7\\). To find \\(a - b\\), we perform the subtraction:\n\\[\na - b = 3 - (-7)\n\\]\n\\[\na - b = 3 + 7\n\\]\n\\[\na - b = 10\n\\]\n\nThus, the final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{10}\n\\]",
