      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "The standard form of the given line is $y = ax + b$.\n\nGiven:\n$(x_1, y_1) = (4, 5)$ and $(x_2, y_2) = (8, 17)$ are on the line.\n\nSubstituting these into the equation:\n\\[5 = 4a + b\\]\n\\[17 = 8a + b\\]\n\nWe need to solve the system of linear equations:\n\\[\n\\begin{cases}\n4a + b = 5 \\\\\n8a + b = 17\n\\end{cases}\n\\]\n\nSubtract the first equation from the second to find the value of $a$:\n\\[\n(8a + b) - (4a + b) = 17 - 5\n\\]\n\\[4a = 12\\]\n\\[a = 3\\]\n\nNext, we substitute $a = 3$ back into one of the original equations to solve for $b$:\n\\[4(3) + b = 5\\]\n\\[12 + b = 5\\]\n\\[b = 5 - 12\\]\n\\[b = -7\\]\n\nFinally, calculate $a - b$:\n\\[a - b = 3 - (-7) = 3 + 7 = 10\\]\n\nThus, the final answer is $\\boxed{10}$.",
