      "text": "1. **Substitute the points into the line equation:**\n   Given that the line \\( y = ax + b \\) passes through the points \\((4,5)\\) and \\((8,17)\\), we can substitute these points into the equation to find \\(a\\) and \\(b\\).\n\n2. **Using the point \\((4,5)\\):**\n   \\[\n   y = ax + b \\implies 5 = 4a + b\n   \\]\n   So, we have the first equation:\n   \\[\n   4a + b = 5 \\quad \\text{(Equation 1)}\n   \\]\n\n3. **Using the point \\((8,17)\\):**\n   \\[\n   y = ax + b \\implies 17 = 8a + b\n   \\]\n   So, we have the second equation:\n   \\[\n   8a + b = 17 \\quad \\text{(Equation 2)}\n   \\]\n\n4. **Solve the system of linear equations:**\n   Subtract Equation 1 from Equation 2 to eliminate \\(b\\):\n   \\[\n   (8a + b) - (4a + b) = 17 - 5\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   8a + b - 4a - b = 12\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   4a = 12\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   a = 3\n   \\]\n\n5. **Substitute \\(a = 3\\) back into Equation 1 to find \\(b\\):**\n   \\[\n   4(3) + b = 5\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   12 + b = 5\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   b = 5 - 12\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   b = -7\n   \\]\n\n6. **Calculate \\(a - b\\):**\n   \\[\n   a - b = 3 - (-7)\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   a - b = 3 + 7\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   a - b = 10\n   \\]\n\nThe final answer is \\(\\boxed{10}\\).",
